{"results": [{"id": "FAM:SF-APPM-058", "label": "Study family SF-APPM-058: PNR shot-level season rates vs possession labels", "score": 1.226, "reached_via": ["request matches the question or hypothesis of FAM:SF-APPM-058 (0.76)", "request matches RQC:RQC-069 (0.73); FAM:SF-APPM-058 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-069"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "PNR shot-level season rates vs possession labels", "auto_outcome_status": "not a hypothesis test", "observed_hypothesis": "PBP-derived shot-level PNR rates sit in a realistic band (script notes possession-level rates will be higher) and vary by team as expected.", "observed_result": "2024-25 shot-level PNR share of half-court shots ranges from OKC 7.567% (498/6581) and BOS 7.854% to IND 13.824% (856/6192) and NYK 11.959%. ATL 11.361%, DEN 11.404%, PHX 10.232% (bh 7.050 / roll 3.181).", "auto_failure_mechanism": "E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)", "observed_failure_evidence": "No pass/fail gate in the output; rates are a calibration input for PBPProxyPNR (later logs show calibrated PNR ~17.9-19.6% of possessions).", "observed_sample_and_power": "30 teams, half_court_shots ~5994-6581", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPM-014"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-035", "label": "Study family SF-APPA-035: Relative-structure single-game validation BOS vs OKC", "score": 1.183, "reached_via": ["FAM:SF-APPA-063 auto_related_family (repeat_order_unknown) FAM:SF-APPA-035", "FAM:SF-APPA-063 auto_related_family (repeat_order_unknown) FAM:SF-APPA-035"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Relative-structure single-game validation BOS vs OKC", "auto_outcome_status": "untestable", "observed_hypothesis": "Model's top-ranked play types score above team average in a held-out game.", "observed_result": "BOS rho 0.200, top-3 n/a, bottom-3 1/3; OKC rho 0.543, top-3 2/2, lift +0.308, bottom-3 1/3.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)", "observed_failure_evidence": "One game; 5-6 PTs per team with 4-35 possessions.", "observed_sample_and_power": "1 game", "auto_validation_status": "same_pipeline_validation; evidence: APPA-035: 'one holdout game 0022400946; spearman of predicted vs actual pt ppp (pt'", "observed_method": "One holdout game 0022400946; Spearman of predicted vs actual PT PPP (PTs >=3 poss); top-3/bottom-3 hits.", "observed_verdict": "inconclusive", "observed_failure_type": "A_unanswerable", "observed_notes": "NOT_RECORDED"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPA-063"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-063", "label": "Study family SF-APPA-063: Holdout play-type rank validation (LAYER_AUDIT)", "score": 0.788, "reached_via": ["request matches the question or hypothesis of FAM:SF-APPA-063 (0.79)"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Holdout play-type rank validation (LAYER_AUDIT)", "auto_outcome_status": "supported", "observed_hypothesis": "Pre-game PT PPP ranking from training data correlates with actual efficiency ranking in held-out games.", "observed_result": "Median rho +0.539 (IQR +0.245 to +0.750); 62.4% rho>0.4; 88.4% rho>0; 10.5% rho<0. Top-3 median hit 100%; >=2/3 hits 78.9%; median lift +0.4261 PPP; 90.8% positive lift. Bottom-3 median suppression 66.7%. MAE cited in la [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Doc caveat: top-3 lift partly reflects league-wide high-efficiency PTs (CUT, PUTBACK, TRANSITION); 10.5% of rows the model misleads (rho<0).", "observed_sample_and_power": "908 game-team rows; 454 games"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPA-035"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-011", "label": "Study family SF-APPS-011: Regular season vs playoff PPP by play type (DRIVE over-prediction)", "score": 0.784, "reached_via": ["request matches the question or hypothesis of FAM:SF-APPS-011 (0.78)"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Regular season vs playoff PPP by play type (DRIVE over-prediction)", "auto_outcome_status": "supported", "observed_hypothesis": "DRIVE PPP is materially higher in RS than playoffs, so an RS-calibrated optimizer over-recommends DRIVE.", "observed_result": "DRIVE RS 1.198 vs PO 0.912 (-0.286, 25 teams); PNR -0.173; PULL_UP +0.301; others within -0.07.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "D_positive (no failure: positive result)", "observed_failure_evidence": "DRIVE playoff PPP 0.286 below RS across 25 teams; top-10 teams all -0.30 to -0.43.", "observed_sample_and_power": "25 teams, min 30 poss per cell; no CIs", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_method": "Team-level (team, PT, context) cells, min 30 poss, up to 25 teams.", "observed_verdict": "supported", "observed_failure_type": "D_positive", "observed_notes": "Motivated the playoff DRIVE exclusion and a proposed playoff DSI offset."}, "relationships": []}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPM-044", "label": "Study family SF-APPM-044: Live-blog game replays: LP BEST/AVOID tier accuracy", "score": 0.77, "reached_via": ["request matches the question or hypothesis of FAM:SF-APPM-044 (0.77)"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Live-blog game replays: LP BEST/AVOID tier accuracy", "auto_outcome_status": "inconclusive", "observed_hypothesis": "Pre-game LP BEST/AVOID tiers predict in-game play-type PPP (scored only on BEST/AVOID, not OK).", "observed_result": "0042500104 and 0042500173: Final 0-0, no classified possessions. 0042500101 DET 96-ORL 108: DET 2/3 (67%), ORL 2/4 (50%); ORL AVOID share 50/79 (63%). 0042500111 BOS 123-PHI 90: BOS 3/4 (75%), PHI 2/3 (67%). 0042500114 B [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Two of six replays had no classified possessions; remaining games mixed 50-75% tier accuracy with frequent AVOID live-overrides (model wrong, engine caught it).", "observed_sample_and_power": "n=6 games; scored cells 3-6 BEST/AVOID per team"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:small_sample"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-058", "label": "Study family SF-APPA-058: Season stability of top suppressors and negative teammate pairs", "score": 0.476, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-044 (0.75); FAM:SF-APPA-058 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-044"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Season stability of top suppressors and negative teammate pairs", "auto_outcome_status": "rejected", "observed_hypothesis": "Each star's top sequential suppressor is stable across seasons, and some teammate X->Y sequences have large negative premiums.", "observed_result": "2/30 (7%) stable (>=75% same top suppressor): D. Mitchell PUTBACK 75%, L. James POST_UP 75%. Negative: J. Tatum->K. Porzingis DRIVE->SPOT_UP -0.444 n=31; Giannis->Lillard DRIVE->PNR -0.263 n=31; J. Brown->J. Tatum SPOT_U [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "B_powered_null (adequately powered null result)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Only 2/30 stars meet the 75% same-top-suppressor stability rule.", "observed_sample_and_power": "30 stars x 4 seasons; min n=20/cell", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_verdict": "null"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:small_sample"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-058", "label": "Study family SF-APPS-058: Observed on-ball defensive scheme labels (ORL-DET G1)", "score": 0.471, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-079 (0.75); FAM:SF-APPS-058 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-079"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Observed on-ball defensive scheme labels (ORL-DET G1)", "auto_outcome_status": "untestable", "observed_hypothesis": "NBA matchup/PBP fields can label on-ball coverage (DROP/ICE/SWITCH) at usable rates.", "observed_result": "DET: 67 on-ball HC poss, 10 labeled (14.9%) ? DROP n=5 PPP=1.20, ICE_CANDIDATE n=5 PPP=0.80, OTHER n=57 PPP=1.42. ORL: 60 poss, 2 labeled (3.3%). switches_on unpopulated.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Confident label rates 14.9% and 3.3%; NBA matchups feed did not populate switches_on.", "observed_sample_and_power": "n=67/60 possessions, 10/2 labeled", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_verdict": "failed_gate"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:label_or_classification_error"}, {"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:small_sample"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:LABEL_ERROR"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-CHT-025", "label": "Study family SF-CHT-025: Play-type labeling audit: OTHER/DRIVE foul leakage", "score": 0.463, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-087 (0.73); FAM:SF-CHT-025 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-087"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Play-type labeling audit: OTHER/DRIVE foul leakage", "auto_outcome_status": "artifact", "observed_hypothesis": "Play-type PPP differences are real efficiency, not labeling/foul artifacts.", "observed_result": "OTHER: 36% end in fouls, PPP inflated (FOUL_BUCKET). DRIVE: 12pp below foul benchmark (FOUL_LEAK). PNR shows 22% foul rate. Only 335 of 50,668 possessions (0.7%) map to a real play type via initiation_type.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)", "observed_failure_evidence": "OTHER PPP inflated by 36% foul endings; DRIVE 12pp below foul benchmark; initiation_type maps 0.7%.", "observed_sample_and_power": "50,668 possessions in the initiation_type check", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_method": "Per-PT diagnostic of foul-ending share vs PPP; initiation_type mapping.", "observed_verdict": "artifact_found"}, "relationships": []}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-056", "label": "Study family SF-APPA-056: TRANSITION gradient subgroup on four pace-sensitive stars", "score": 0.46, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-043 (0.73); FAM:SF-APPA-056 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-043"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "TRANSITION gradient subgroup on four pace-sensitive stars", "auto_outcome_status": "untestable", "observed_hypothesis": "For stars whose #1 sequential suppressor is TRANSITION (Tatum, Morant, Young, Haliburton), TRANSITION hits hardest in Q1 then adapts by Q4, unlike PUTBACK.", "observed_result": "TRANSITION Q1 d=-0.221 (n=352) to Q4 d=-0.146 (n=262), gradient +0.075. PUTBACK compounds -0.067; POST_UP compounds -0.098. T. Young exception Q1 -0.023 to Q4 -0.240.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)", "observed_failure_evidence": "4-star subgroup selected on the outcome (TRANSITION is already their #1 suppressor); full 30-star TRANSITION gradient is only -0.053.", "observed_sample_and_power": "4 stars; TRANSITION Q1 n=352 / Q4 n=262", "observed_verdict": "inconclusive", "auto_confidence": "high (1.0)"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:RTM_SELECTION"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-CHT-009", "label": "Study family SF-CHT-009: Superstar suppression by lineup and forced play type", "score": 0.46, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-083 (0.73); FAM:SF-CHT-009 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-083"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Superstar suppression by lineup and forced play type", "auto_outcome_status": "not a hypothesis test", "observed_hypothesis": "Named star initiators have identifiable lineup and forced-play-type suppressors in the possession graph.", "observed_result": "Jokic vs MIN lineup PPP 0.814, -0.385 (n=59); Curry vs HOU 0.851, -0.358 (n=47); Doncic vs LAC 0.733, -0.396 (n=30); Giannis forced PULL_UP 0.848, -0.540 vs preferred DRIVE (largest gap).", "auto_failure_mechanism": "E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)", "observed_failure_evidence": "No placebo or matching; later sequence work treated similar star-chain gaps as artifacts.", "observed_sample_and_power": "n>=30 for lineup cells cited", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_method": "Jokic/Curry/Doncic/Giannis; min-15 gate on 8 play types; opposing DEFENSE_LINEUP ~84% coverage; 272-row CSV."}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:PLACEBO_DEPENDENCE"}]}], "n_results": 10}

Stage 2. Using the retrieval result above (follow-up tools are allowed within the tool budget), complete steps 4 to 9
and reply with the final action. Output schema (all fields required):
{
 "research_concepts": [
  "concept"
 ],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "question"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a record returned by a tool",
   "status_as_recorded": "outcome status exactly as stated in the record (supported | rejected | inconclusive | untestable | artifact | not a hypothesis test | no result recorded)",
